# ── 2026-08-10 sync: health 2.6, clinical 1.14, coverage 1.4, checkup 3.3,
#    core 3.5. Released in SDK 2.0.0. ──
#
# health=2.6 / clinical=1.14: interpretation is no longer a five-word set this
#     project invented. LAB_INTERPRETATION_VALUES carries the 49 SELECTABLE codes
#     of HL7 v3 ObservationInterpretation 3.0.0 (the code system FHIR R4 binds
#     Observation.interpretation to) in the code system's own order, plus the
#     data-absent-reason code "unknown" and the ten retained legacy words: 60
#     values. LabInterpretation is DERIVED from that array, so the type and the
#     runtime list cannot drift. The list is pinned by a SHA-256 recomputed in
#     test rather than by reading the shape file, because this package's CI
#     checks out no spec sibling and a test that skipped itself when its input
#     was missing would report green while proving nothing.
#     Two pre-existing defects are corrected by the same change: "elevated" was a
#     member of the union and was never accepted by any version of the shapes,
#     and "high" was accepted by every version and was missing from the union.
# health=2.6 / clinical=1.14: labCategory, testCode, icd10Code and snomedCode are
#     0..*. FHIR R4 Observation.category is 0..* and CodeableConcept.coding is
#     0..*, so a record that preserved every coding its source sent was being
#     rejected for preserving it. Represented as MultiValue<string> (a bare value
#     or an array) and handled ARITY-PRESERVINGLY on both sides: N values in
#     produce N repeated-predicate triples, N triples read back as N values, and
#     one value still round-trips as a bare string. Uniform by FIELD NAME across
#     every model that carries one of the four, because the serializer resolves
#     the namespace per record type but decides cardinality before it has any
#     type context, and no shape still caps any of the four at one.
#     NOT an rdf:List: the vocabulary declares no order and the shapes count
#     triples. The JSON-LD context keeps these terms plain rather than declaring
#     @container: @set, because @set means "always an array on compaction" and
#     this SDK emits a bare value for a single coding.
# coverage=1.4: SubscriberRelationship completed to the full HL7
#     SubscriberPolicyholder code system that FHIR R4 Coverage.relationship binds
#     to (child, parent, spouse, common, other, self, injured). v1.4 added common
#     and injured; parent had been missing here since the type was introduced.
#     The other v1.4 change relaxes coverage:coverageType from a closed list to an
#     advisory warning, matching FHIR's EXTENSIBLE binding; this SDK already typed
#     that field `CoverageType | string` and rejects nothing, so it needed no
#     change to be conformant.
# checkup=3.3: SHACL only. An icd10Code sh:pattern that required a digit in the
#     second and third characters, so live categories with a letter there (C4A,
#     D3A, M1A) failed. This SDK validates no lexical patterns and models no
#     checkup: class, so there is nothing here for the fix to change. The row is
#     bumped because 3.3 adds no term this SDK is missing, not because code moved.
# core=3.5: cascade:sourceIdentity, the ORIGIN axis: a canonical,
#     transport-independent identity for the organization a record came from, so
#     a FHIR export and a C-CDA document of one health system agree. Registered
#     as a predicate, carried in the generated JSON-LD context as a plain term
#     (matching the published context), and typed on CascadeEntity because its
#     rdfs:domain is owl:Thing. Values are scheme-prefixed org: / ns: /
#     transport:; the accessor is a plain optional string and this SDK does NOT
#     validate or derive the scheme. Minting a slug requires the source document,
#     which only an importer has, and rejecting an unrecognized value here would
#     discard origin information a producer was entitled to write.
#     cascade:sourceSystem, whose comment narrowed in the same version, is still
#     unregistered here and remains a gap.

# core=3.6: cascade:dataAbsentReason registered and in the generated context;
#     the serializer dropped it entirely before. cascade:sourceSystem
#     registered too: it has been in the published context since core v3.0 and
#     was never registered here, so the INGESTION axis could not round-trip
#     while ORIGIN could.
# health=2.7 / clinical=1.15: interpretationSourceCode registered in BOTH
#     spellings (health: on labs, clinical: on vitals) and typed on VitalSign
#     AND on LabResult, as MultiValue<string>. The arity is the writer's and the
#     reader's: a triple per value out, every triple back, so a model saying
#     `string` described data this SDK does not produce and a caller's
#     `.trim()` typechecked and threw. sh:maxCount 1 on both shapes is a rule
#     about validating a graph, not about what a reader may find in one.
#     LAB_INTERPRETATION_VALUES moves 60 to 74 (the 14 data-absent-reason codes
#     it lacked) and the checksum is re-pinned. VitalSign.interpretation
#     narrows from `VitalInterpretation | string`, which TypeScript collapsed
#     to `string`: clinical v1.15 binds the vital shape, so the open binding
#     that justified the union is gone. Procedure records retarget onto
#     clinical:Procedure / clinical:procedureName, with health:procedureName
#     registered so a name carried only on the deprecated spelling survives.

